isSupportedInZeroLocus -- whether support of a module is contained in the zero locus of the (irrelevant) ideal
**************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isSupportedInZeroLocus_B M
  * Inputs:
      * B, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * M, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a *note module:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, or a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if $M$ (or $R^1/I$,
        if an ideal of $R$ is given) is supported only on the zero locus of
        $B$; that is, whether $\mathrm{supp}(M) \subset \mathrm{V}(B)$

Description
===========

Given an module $M$ and an ideal $B$, isSupportedInZeroLocus checks whether
$\mathrm{ann}(M):B^\infty=R$. If it is, isSupportedInZeroLocus returns true
otherwise it returns false. If the second argument is an ideal, $M = R^1/I$ is
taken as the module.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/32003[x_0..x_4, Degrees=>{2:{1,0}, 3:{0,1}}];|
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : irr = intersect(ideal(x_0,x_1), ideal(x_2,x_3,x_4));|
|                                                         |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = S^1/(irr^2);                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isSupportedInZeroLocus_irr M                        |
|                                                         |
|o4 = true                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

This is done without computing saturation of $M$. Instead, we check whether for
each generator of $B$ some power of it annihilates the module $M$.

Ways to use isSupportedInZeroLocus:
===================================

  * "isSupportedInZeroLocus(Ideal,Complex)"
  * "isSupportedInZeroLocus(Ideal,Ideal)"
  * "isSupportedInZeroLocus(Ideal,Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isSupportedInZeroLocus: isSupportedInZeroLocus, is a *note
method function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

